  "comment": "The ice world's tileset, cut from artwork/tiles/ice.png, and the maps drawn with it. Pieces are rectangles in pixels, [x, y, w, h]: x and y on the 8 px grid, w and h in 16s (one block or more, row-major). Transparent pixels become the backdrop colour (snow). Maps are rows of legend characters, one per block; a piece bigger than a block is drawn by repeating its character over its whole size ('stretch': a run of any length, the piece's first and last blocks at its ends). tools/tileset.mjs fits it all to the Color and writes build/gen/tiles_ice.c (docs/design/art-pipeline.md).",
